{
  "notes": "Candidate outcomes for free exploration on the All of Us Registered Tier. Concept ids are standard OMOP ids as best known; verify_catalog() checks each against the CDR concept table (exists, domain, name contains expect_name) and skips any that fail, so a wrong id is reported rather than analysed. Newer entries name their concept by public code (SNOMED, LOINC); resolve_codes() looks the code up in the CDR vocabulary, and the same concept check then applies. Defaults apply to every entry of a kind unless the entry sets the field: a condition case needs diagnoses on two distinct dates (min_occurrences), the usual guard against rule-out codes. The phenome scan (codas/aou/phenome.py) screens every verified entry against every wearable feature on the discovery share and selects outcomes by their hits, so the catalog is meant to be broad: diagnoses across organ systems and common lab values, each by its public code.",
  "defaults": {
    "condition": {
      "min_occurrences": 2
    }
  },
